Ey=dN,kEz=[0,ci,[0,g,beM]],kEA=eG,kEB=[0,cd,[0,g,eG]],kEJ=[0,1],kEI=dp,kEH=dp,kEG=dp,kEF=m,kEE=fJ,kED="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",kEK=[0,m],kEL=[0,j4],kEN=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],kEO=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],kEP=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],kEQ=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],kER=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],kES=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],kET=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],kEU=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],kEV=[0,0,0],kEW=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],kEX=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],kEZ=[0,m,0],kE0=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],kE1=kV(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),kE3=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],kE9=[0,m],kE8="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",kE7="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",kE6="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",kE4="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",kFe=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],kFd=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],kFf=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],kFc=[0,"Empty hole"],kFb=hj,kFa=[0,"Missing operator"],kE_=[0,0,1],kE$=[0,0,0],kFg=[0,[0,kS,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jp]],[0,[0,j7,[0,R,[0,[0,k8,[0,R,[0,n0g,n0f]]],0]]],[0,[0,hI,[0,h,[0,[0,g,k8],0]]],0]]]]],0],kFh=dN,kFi=[0,ci,[0,g,bhE]],kFj=eG,kFk=[0,cd,[0,g,eG]],kFl=[0,[0,kS,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jp]],[0,[0,j7,[0,R,[0,[0,k8,[0,R,[0,n0i,n0h]]],0]]],[0,[0,hI,[0,h,[0,[0,g,k8],0]]],0]]]]],0],kFm=dN,kFn=[0,ci,[0,g,bfb]],kFo=eG,kFp=[0,cd,[0,g,eG]],kFq=[0,[0,kS,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,g,jp]],[0,[0,j7,[0,R,[0,[0,k8,[0,R,[0,n0k,n0j]]],0]]],[0,[0,hI,[0,h,[0,[0,g,k8],0]]],0]]]]],0],kFr=dN,kFs=[0,ci,[0,g,bdD]],kFt=eG,kFu=[0,cd,[0,g,eG]],kFK=[0,1],kFH=[0,Kc],kFI=[0,dp],kFJ=fJ,kFF=[0,40],kFE=[0,HF],kFG=m,kFD=[0,0],kFy=[0,1],kFz=[0,m],kFA=[0,j4],kFB=dp,kFC=fJ,kFv=bgj,kFw=dv8,kFx=bTd,kFL=[0,0],kFP=[0,0],kFR=[0,1],kFQ=[0,m],kGg="Warning: using backup text! Serialization may be for an older version of Hazel.",kGe="persistence load",kGf="PARSE FAILED (persistence load): loading empty buffer",kGb=[0,1],kGc=[0,0],kGd=[0,0],kGa=m,kFS=[0,[18,[1,[0,[11,b,0],b]],[11,aY,0]],a0],kFT=sY,kFU=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,A,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],B],kFV=[0,[3,0,0],aJ],kFW=[0,[17,0,0],z],kFX=[0,[12,59,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]],C],kFY=afE,kFZ=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,A,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],B],kF0=[0,[3,0,0],aJ],kF1=[0,[17,0,0],z],kF2=[0,[17,[0,a,1,0],[12,aG,[17,0,0]]],a2],kF_=afE,kF$=sY,kF8=afE,kF9=sY,kF6=[0,afE],kF7=[0,sY],kF4=afE,kF5=sY,kF3=dTm,kGh=".*\\)::$",kGm=fJ,kGl=[0,0,0],kGk=ss,kGi=m,kGj=m,kHG="ChatLSP: term_string_of: Secondary",kHF=[0,[11,"Error in term:\n  ",[2,0,[11,"\nNature of error: ",[2,0,0]]]],"Error in term:\n  %s\nNature of error: %s"],kHE=Kg,kHy=Kg,kHz=Kg,kHA=m,kHB=Kg,kHC=m,k